From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shariq Khalil Ahmed <shariq.ahmed@cohere.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:48:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Link OpenSSL through openssl-sys

Intel's packaged libsgx_dcap_quoteverify.so links the system OpenSSL
itself. A statically built copy needs OpenSSL from whoever links it, and
should use the same one as the rest of the process: in the cohere-tng
wheel, the copy openssl/vendored builds and links statically.

Depend on openssl-sys for that, which also gives the build script
OpenSSL's headers (DEP_OPENSSL_INCLUDE). Name the crate in lib.rs, since
rustc does not link a dependency no Rust code refers to.
---
 Cargo.toml | 4 ++++
 src/lib.rs | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 5e4c1cc..b05b66c 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -12,6 +12,10 @@ homepage = "https://github.com/intel/confidential-computing.tee.dcap"
 # See more keys and their definitions at https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/manifest.html
 
 [dependencies]
+# Not called from Rust: the library calls OpenSSL, and linking it through openssl-sys puts it
+# on the same OpenSSL as the rest of the process (vendored in the wheel). openssl-sys also
+# hands its include directory to build.rs as DEP_OPENSSL_INCLUDE.
+openssl-sys = "0.9"
 
 [build-dependencies]
 bindgen = "0.70.1"
diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 8ba7aae..7189a05 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -51,4 +51,8 @@
 // `# Safety` doc sections; suppress the lint for the generated file.
 #![allow(clippy::missing_safety_doc)]
 
+// Only the C library uses OpenSSL, and rustc drops a dependency no Rust code names, which
+// would leave OpenSSL off the link line.
+use openssl_sys as _;
+
 include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/bindings.rs"));
